WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.567
We continue to

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.768
follow breaking news for you

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.402
this morning.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.536
Just frightening scenes

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.671
coming out of Japan

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.739
on this New Year's Day.

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:06.806
Japan's West Coast

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:10.076
reeling after a powerful 7.5 magnitude

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:10.910
quake caused

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.045
widespread damage,

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.346
triggered tsunami warnings

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.348
and four foot tsunami waves.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.950
This is the moment that the quake struck

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.318
just a few hours ago.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.185
You see that building

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.887
crumbling to the ground

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.355
On the screens, upper left side there.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.523
And take a look at the scene

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:26.559
from inside of an office building

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:27.794
in

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:43.243
That's the first time

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.144
I'm seeing this video.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:44.544
You can see

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.945
just how long it goes on

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:49.082
and just how violent that shaking is.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.451
Houses have collapsed.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.553
We have seen pictures of roofs there

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.622
just fallen down.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.122
The earthquake

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.758
also caused fires in some areas.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:00:59.793
And at this moment,

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.095
tsunami warnings do remain in effect.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.630
They have been downgraded.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.531
You can see

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.465
the initial impact

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:06.966
of one of these tsunamis,

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.334
one of these small waves there.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.602
It doesn't look like much,

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.671
but this can be a threat,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.574
particularly if you get repeated waves.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:15.542
The warnings

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:18.445
now are of waves of up to ten feet

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.947
We have full team coverage for you.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:21.514
CNN's Kanako

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.049
Montgomery is in Tokyo,

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.717
Derek Van Dam at the weather center.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.885
And I go first to you.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.487
What are you hearing at this point

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.588
from the Japanese government

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.226
Yeah, John.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.727
So right now it's currently

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.629
nighttime in Japan,

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.897
so we're still waiting to confirm

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.432
a lot of outstanding questions

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.968
about the extent of the devastation

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.069
from the earthquake

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.771
and subsequent tsunami.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.772
But what we do know

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:46.139
is that

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:49.442
33,000 homes in Ishikawa Prefecture,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.411
which is very close to the epicenter,

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.313
have lost power.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.380
We also know that bullet

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.449
train lines have been suspended.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.518
Some roads have had cracks in them,

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.719
making it very difficult

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.753
for emergency

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.123
medical personnel to get to survivors.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.891
We also know that fires

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.326
have broken out across

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.128
Ishikawa Prefecture

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.863
and a thousand self-defense

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.965
force personnel have been dispatched

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.234
to aid in evacuation efforts.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:17.003
This is along with 1700 firefighters

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.039
also to help in evacuation efforts.

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.040
Now, 20

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.142
self-defense force

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.644
aircrafts are also monitoring the area

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.311
to just

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.446
try to get a sense

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.581
of the extent of this devastation.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:29.582
Now, also,

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.617
I just want to point out

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.719
that this did happen on New Year's Day,

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:33.153
a time

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.387
when many people

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.455
are celebrating New Year's

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.290
with their families in their homes,

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.491
with their loved ones.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:41.294
And when this quake hit at 4:10 p.m.,

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:43.830
that initial quake hit at 4:10 p.m.,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.331
it shocked the entire country.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.933
People were forced to leave their homes,

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.101
leave their belongings

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.103
and evacuate to higher ground.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:50.570
Of course,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.038
the aftershocks

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:52.906
that followed soon

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.041
afterwards were also very powerful.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:55.475
And it's

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:58.211
reminding a lot of people of the 2011

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.847
Tohoku earthquake and tsunami

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.116
because of just how long the quakes are.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.018
How the tsunami warnings

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.452
have also been issued, John.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.321
And just really a lot of fear

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.088
and just

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.056
lots to confirm

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.192
about the extent of devastation

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.460
really early days into sort of

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.529
assessing the damage. Hanako, thank you.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.997
Let me bring Derek into the conversation.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:18.865
Derek as we just said,

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:19.999
we know the tsunami warnings

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.434
have been downgraded.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.502
But help us understand

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.770
practically what that means.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.672
I mean, what is the risk right now?

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.008
Well, John, what you're seeing

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.577
is some really stunning

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:31.411
new video

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.813
coming out of the Ishikawa Prefecture.

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.015
This this is new to us.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.418
And you're looking at Suzhou City, Japan.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.385
So this is on the opposite

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.654
side of the peninsula

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.356
and just zooming in.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.391
What you're looking at is a brick wall.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.626
Some of the seawall here, we're

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.094
analyzing this video on the fly.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.363
So it's a bit tricky to establish

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.464
exactly what's going on.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.298
But we believe that

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.633
this is the moment

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:54.300
the tsunami,

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.636
the initial tsunami wave impacted

00:03:56.636 --> 00:04:00.506
this part of the Ishikawa Prefecture.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.574
And you can see the water

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.876
kind of pummeling over that seawall,

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:04.744
which we would have to

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:05.612
guess here

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.280
is several meters high

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.548
if it's protecting the harbor.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:09.482
But you can see the waves

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:12.018
splashing up into the populated areas.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.053
I'm going to reset my graphics here

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:14.821
and just give a little bit

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.222
more of an indication of

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:18.091
where exactly this is.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.927
We've zoomed in to Suzhou City

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.129
and there is that breakwater wall.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.998
This is the population area.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:25.865
And again,

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.634
this is on the opposite side

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:28.635
of where

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:30.136
the magnitude 7.5

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.738
earthquake actually occurred.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:32.939
So we're getting

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.375
some profound video of the tsunami wave

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:36.909
that has actually moved in

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.344
and you could see

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.279
other areas there

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:41.848
fitting that narrative of waves over

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:42.382
four feet

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.550
in some instances, with tsunami warnings

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.853
still ongoing across those Western

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.187
Asian shorelines

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.023
of the country of Japan,

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.691
particularly across the Honshu region.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:53.660
All right.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.228
Derek Van Dam, thanks to you.

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.796
Hanako Montgomery who is in Tokyo.

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.264
Our thanks to both of you.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.599
Let's continue the conversation now.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.200
Joining us now is Robert Geller.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.302
He is a seismologist

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:02.835
and emeritus

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:05.071
professor at the University of Tokyo.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.806
Robert good to have you today.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.941
Can I just ask I mean, you are in Tokyo.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.877
Did you feel the earthquake?

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:11.811
Can you share with us

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:14.580
what your experience was?

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.783
Well, I felt the earthquake,

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:20.353
but only very, very low level shaking.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.723
I had the TV on and on.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:28.895
No warnings of an imminent earthquake

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.565
striking a prefecture.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:36.302
Where would repeat in on a loop

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.971
over and over again with the kind of horn

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.374
