00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:41.908
So not

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:43.409
that was very dramatic,

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.010
but actually,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.079
you could hardly feel anything in Tokyo.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:47.046
Well, that's

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.481
really interesting in the video

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:49.082
that we're showing.

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:49.449
I'm not sure

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.150
if you can see the screen right now,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.418
but the video is also quite

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:53.720
dramatic monitors

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.055
and office buildings really shaking

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:57.523
from from their perspective.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.991
What is the biggest risk right now?

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.526
What are you watching right now?

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.364
Well, there are tourists slow.

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.998
One is the buildings

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:07.800
that have collapsed

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.902
or partially collapsed.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:11.904
If there are people trapped in them,

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.140
all the emergency forces

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.310
have about 48 hours to get the people out

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.879
or mostly it's too late.

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.181
So so that's a race against time.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:22.782
And I'm sure

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:26.219
the firemen and self-defense forces

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.588
will do the best they can.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:31.124
The second risk

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:33.693
is there's a very small problem

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.295
it may be only one or 2%

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.530
that you could have

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.599
an even bigger earthquake

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:42.101
in the next week or two.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:45.004
There sure to be aftershocks,

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:47.173
but almost all the time

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:49.442
they're smaller than the main shock.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:52.044
So the aftershocks will only be

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:53.646
a problem

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:54.380
for buildings

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.215
that have already been damaged

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:58.584
and then any little further block in

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.919
the march them.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.721
But if you have a bigger earthquake

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:03.189
that could really be a problem

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:05.491
is not very likely,

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:08.161
but it's not impossible right now.

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:09.962
Non-zero percent chance

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:10.930
we're talking about here.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.732
Some people do need to be on alert.

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:14.834
We have seen some images

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:17.103
of some of the smaller waves.

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:20.306
The initial tsunamis that did did occur

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:20.907
from this.

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:22.141
There are still warnings in effect

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.444
for waves of up to ten feet high.

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:25.645
How long do you think

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:27.246
people need to be on alert

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:28.181
for the water there?

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.651
Well, the

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.586
flow from the main shock

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:36.656
probably not that much longer.

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:37.757
I think

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:38.991
perhaps the government

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:41.160
is being a little overly cautious

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:44.464
bearing in mind what happened in 2011

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:47.033
when you know

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:48.434
it's one of these better safe

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:49.502
than sorry things

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:50.736
if people

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:53.673
stay away from their homes for 24 hours

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:57.944
that's probably not such a bad

00:07:57.944 --> 00:07:58.711
thing.

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.780
Just in case.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.182
Extra precautions certainly in order

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:05.251
given what happened in 2011

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:06.252
and the severity of this quake.

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:08.521
It was a very powerful earthquake.

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:10.623
Still assessing the damage from Professor

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:11.224
Robert Keller

